                 DIGITAL INTRODUCES INDUSTRY-LEADING
                          PORTABLE PRINTER


       Smallest, Lightest-Weight Portable Ink Jet Strengthens
              Digital's Challenge to Market Competitors


LAS VEGAS, Nevada -- November 14, 1994 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation continues to aggressively challenge its competitors in 
the printer market with today's introduction of the industry's 
smallest, lightest-weight portable ink jet printer.  The DECwriter 
90ip printer features a compact size of 11.6" (h) x 5.2" (w) x 2.5" 
(d) and weighs just 2.4 pounds.  The latest addition to Digital's 
growing line of desktop/personal printers, the DECwriter 90ip 
printer is designed to help increase productivity by enabling 
workers, in virtually any environment, to quickly generate quality 
output.  The announcement was made at COMDEX, which opened here 
today at the Las Vegas Convention Center.

     "Today's announcement reinforces Digital's commitment to 
strengthening its position in the competitive printer market," said 
Larry Cabrinety, Vice President, Components and Periphers Unit.  
"Over the last month we have effectively challenged industry 
leaders, expanded our diverse offering of printer solutions, and 
increased our presence in the retail and distribution channels."

     Portable printing is currently a rapidly expanding segment of 
the computing industry.  According to market research, transportable 
printers accounted for 10.8% of all U.S. printer market shipments in 
1993.1   Digital's DECwriter 90ip portable printer is a reliable and 
ideal solution for business travelers and those who take work home, 
to generate critical output, such as last minute slides for a 
presentation, and quickly add information to proposals, contracts 
and more.  It is especially appropriate for optimizing the mobile 
computing environments of sales, insurance, real estate and banking 
personnel.

     The DECwriter 90ip printer features a print speed of 2 pages-
per-minute, 300 x 300 dpi resolution for high-quality printing, and 
an integral auto sheet feeder that holds up to 15 sheets of paper so 
no manual loading is required.  The printer's battery or AC power 
operation allows for complete portability and convenience.  In 
addition, the DECwriter 90ip printer ships with a Windows 3.1 
driver, HP PCL-3 emulation and a parallel interface for PC 
compatibility, and is EPA Energy Star compliant.  

     "Digital is committed to enabling its customers to print 
wherever they work," said Dave Sweeney, vice president, Digital's 
Printer Business.  "We will continue to deliver industry leading 
printers that meet the evolving needs of today's computing 
environments."  

Pricing and Availability

     Suggested list price for the DECwriter 90ip printer is $340.  
The DECwriter 90ip printer is scheduled to be available through 
Digital's U.S. retail partners.  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
