              THREE NEW AdvantageCluster CONFIGURATIONS
       FROM DIGITAL LEAD INDUSTRY IN SINGLE SYSTEM PERFORMANCE


              ...Expands Digital UNIX cluster family...


WASHINGTON, DC -- November 14, 1994 -- Supercomputing '94 -- Digital
Equipment Corporation today announced the newest members of its
AdvantageCluster family of compute servers. The three new systems 
are enhanced versions of AdvantageCluster 2000, 3000 and 5000 
models.  Designed to meet the needs of customers with applications 
requiring extremely high compute power, the new models are 
particularly well suited to high-end design, modeling, simulation 
and numerical analysis applications. 

     "Digital invented clusters, and these newest members of our
AdvantageCluster family deliver the kind of performance leading
scientific and technical users are looking for," said John O'Keefe,
vice president of UNIX systems marketing for Digital. "By building
clustered systems around standard workstation and server systems 
based on the latest Alpha microprocessor technology, we deliver 
tremendous problem solving power at very low cost." 

The new systems are: 

     o 	AdvantageCluster 2000/225 comprised of four servers based on 
        the 225 MHz Alpha microprocessor in a single system 
        delivering 700 Megaflops for $157,000 

     o 	AdvantageCluster 3000/275 made up of four 275 MHz Alpha 
        servers in a single system delivering 1100 Megaflops for 
        $230,000 

     o 	AdvantageCluster 5000/275 featuring four 275 MHz 
        multiprocessor computers in a single system delivering from 
        760 Megaflops to over three Gigaflops beginning at $219,000. 

     "While our standard packaged systems begin at 700 Megaflops in
performance, the flexibility and scalability of the Digital
AdvantageCluster enables expansion to performance levels to 37
GIGAFLOPS and beyond using standard, off-the-shelf systems,
interconnect components and storage devices. This flexibility and
economy is unmatched in the industry," added O'Keefe. 

     The AdvantageCluster compute server family includes Digital's
TechAdvantage suite of parallel development and optimization tools,
PVM, and POLYCENTER system management software factory-installed and
configured. TechAdvantage software provides customers with all the
necessary development tools to create, execute and maintain high
performance applications in C, C++, Fortran 77 and High Performance
Fortran 90. High Performance Fortran 90 simplifies the development 
of applications for parallel processing, allowing customers to reap 
the significant benefits of powerful symmetric multiprocessing and 
cluster systems. 

     "Digital is a clear leader in UNIX cluster technology," said 
O'Keefe.  "Compared to cluster offerings from IBM, SGI, HP and Sun, 
the AdvantageCluster family offers far superior price/performance, 
greater scalability, a much broader range of compute performance, 
and much lower cost of entry. No UNIX cluster configuration on the 
market can touch these systems." 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms,
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations
compete and win in today's global marketplace. 
