                  DIGITAL ANNOUNCES SIX NEW DEALERS
                   FOR TOKEN RING NETWORK PRINTER


PHOENIX, Arizona -- November 6, 1994 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation today announced the addition of six new dealers for its 
PrintGate/32 network printer.  The dealers, CIS Corporation, 
Syracuse, NY (315-455-4788), ComputerDen, Inc., Miami, FL 
(305-594-0200), Computer Parts & Services, Inc., Plymouth, MN 
(612-553-1514), Maintenance Alternatives Corporation, Petaluma, CA 
(707-765-1325), Next Generation Systems, Inc., Clawson, MI 
(810-435-5086), and Transnational, New York, NY (212-489-8710), will 
market and support Digital's network printer into both IBM AS/400 
token ring and Ethernet open systems environments.  The announcement 
was made at the XPLOR '94 Conference, which opened here today at the 
Phoenix Convention Center.

     Digital's PrintGate/32 printer, announced at the XPLOR 
Conference in November, 1993, simultaneously handles print jobs from 
any desktop device in an IBM AS/400 Token Ring, TCP/IP or DECnet 
Ethernet network, whether local or remote, running Novell NetWare, 
Windows NT, AT&T Unison, HP-UX, IBM AIX, Pyramid OSx, SCO UNIX, 
Sequent Dynix, Silicon Graphics IRIS, Solaris, SunOS, UNISYS System 
V, DEC OSF/1 AXP, ULTRIX, OpenVMS (VAX and Alpha AXP) or (via 
PATHWORKS, NetWare or third party products), DOS, OS/2 or Macintosh 
systems.

     BIS Strategic Decisions awarded Digital the Departmental Page 
Printer Award for Multi-Platform Network Technology at their 
conference last December.  "Mixed network environments can maximize 
organizational investment in printers with the PrintGate/32 for 
multi-platform printing," said Julianne Mehegan, Senior Industry 
Analyst for BIS Strategic Decisions when making the award 
announcement.  The PrintGate/32 network printer is the only 
mid-range printer in the industry designed to support both IBM 
AS/400 Token Ring and Ethernet networks simultaneously.  The 
high-speed duplex (two-sided printing) printer handles complex 
documents which contain images and multifont text at 32 pages per 
minute in print volumes up to 150,000 impressions per month.

     It is a departmental printer which handles labels, 
transparencies, letterhead and cutsheet paper in sizes up to 11" X 
17" (B size) or metric A3.  The standard 1500 sheet I/O capacity can 
be optionally expanded to 3500 input, 4550 output.  An optional 
20-bin, lockable, software-addressable output mailbox enables secure 
printing of sensitive, confidential and time-critical information, 
even from remote geographies or while the printer is unattended.  
The printer notifies users of printer and print job status in 
real-time, including start of print job, successful completion of 
print job, out of paper, and more, even from remote geographies.

     "This expansion of Digital's distribution network to six 
dealers who handle IBM AS/400 Token Ring environments is another 
expansion of our channels strategy to target customers who can 
minimize their printing budgets by using network printers which can 
handle all of their computing environments," said Larry Cabrinety, 
Vice President of Digital's Components and Peripherals Business 
Unit. "Only Digital can bridge the IBM AS/400 Token Ring and Ethernet 
environments with a single printer."

     The PrintGate/32 duplex network printer is priced at $30,995 
and is currently available.

