           DIGITAL ANNOUNCES LOW-COST PCI ETHERNET ADAPTER
                            AT COMDEX '94


LAS VEGAS, Nevada -- November 14, 1994 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation is announcing the EtherWORKS Turbo PCI TP, a low-cost 
single-chip adapter for Ethernet twisted-pair networks. It supports 
PCI-based Intel 486, Pentium, and other industry-standard platforms 
as well as Digital's Alpha systems. The adapter's intelligent DMA 
design delivers optimal network performance with very low CPU 
utilization.  Priced at $179, it offers one of the most economical 
network connections for PCI-based clients and servers.

     A full suite of drivers is included -- NetWare 3.x/4.x ODI 
server, NetWare ODI client (DOS and OS/2), Windows NT 3.1 and 3.5 
(Intel and Alpha), Windows for Workgroups V3.11, PATHWORKS, SCO 
UNIX, LAN Manager (DOS and OS/2), OpenVMS, and DEC OSF/1.  

     The EtherWORKS Turbo PCI TP features plug-and-play installation 
and is completely auto configurable. This 32-bit adapter has an 
optimized system interface and two 256 Byte on-chip FIFOs.  It 
supports full duplex Ethernet capability (20 Mb/s). The adapter 
is FCC and CE Class B certified for worldwide use. A limited 
lifetime warranty is available at no additional charge.

     The EtherWORKS Turbo PCI TP is the latest in a series of high 
performance PCI network adapters from Digital. Last month, the 
company announced the industry's first PCI FDDI adapters. 
Digital also offers a PCI Ethernet adapter that supports ThinWire, 
thick wire, and twisted-pair connections.   

     The EtherWORKS Turbo PCI TP will be displayed with Digital's 
full line of Ethernet and FDDI adapters in Booth L4002 at the Las 
Vegas Convention Center at COMDEX '94.

     Digital was one of the first vendors to introduce products that 
support the high-speed capacity of the Peripheral Component 
Interconnect (PCI) Local Bus. The specification for this bus allows 
a maximum data transfer rate of 132 Megabytes per second, more than 
four times that of an EISA bus.  The company continues to be a 
significant contributor to the development of many popular 
networking technologies, including Ethernet, FDDI and ATM LANs, 
network switches, routers, bridges, network adapters, and terminal 
servers. Digital has networked more than 10 million users worldwide.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
