                    SOFTWARE UTILITY BACKGROUNDER


LAS VEGAS, Nevada -- November 15, 1994 -- Today's enterprise-wide, 
multivendor software environments are often like Rube Goldberg 
creations: unwieldy, unproductive and expensive contraptions
that, in spite of the odds, somehow work. 			    

     Today's companies, however, can no longer afford to take a 
Rube-Goldberg approach to managing their software environments. It's 
simply too expensive.  Fully 75 percent of a user's total software 
costs directly relate to managing the distribution, administration 
and support  of that software. Experts say that large companies 
could potentially save millions of dollars a year by managing these 
resources properly. For example, they could realize a 44 percent 
savings in support costs; a 14 percent savings in licensing fees; 
and a 10 percent savings in upgrade costs alone. 

     Software Utility, a comprehensive service offering from Digital 
Equipment Corporation, provides a sensible, flexible and affordable 
way for companies to gain that control over the factors escalating 
the cost and management of their software across their entire 
enterprise. Software Utility is a partnership with customers that 
allows them successfully to meet the challenges of managing their
software and hardware assets in a constantly changing computing 
environment.

These challenges include: 

     o	increasing complexity 
     o	expanding connectivity 
     o	geographic dispersion, especially in global companies 
     o	chaotic growth of multivendor platforms, architectures and 
        application 
     o	growing user base and growing demand among users for new 
        applications 
     o	move to client/server computing and object-oriented 
        licensing
     
     Experts note that this situation will not change. In fact, the 
opposite is true. Heterogeneity will remain the norm. Growing 
numbers of users will continue to demand new applications and to 
require a consequent need for higher level training and support. The 
numbers of remote users at geographically dispersed sites will rise. 
And increasing numbers of sites will seek to move into client/server 
computing. 

     Those companies without an effective way to manage their 
software environment will, most likely, fail to compete effectively. 

   Software Utility gives users the tools to successfully control 
all facets of the software lifecycle -- from acquisition to 
retirement.  Through product, service and capabilities offerings 
that reduce the cost of software ownership by: 

     o	improving software license use and distribution, especially 
        as license practices change
     o	optimizing system management resources
     o  freeing up staff from manual tasks
     o  and decreasing time to order/install software, increase 
        control and productivity by:

     o	centralizing control and reducing complexity 
     o	tracking and reporting on hardware and software 
     o	automating administrative tasks 
     o	integrating software management practices 
     o	and enabling a faster deployment of technology

     Software Utility provides leading-edge tools and services to 
help customers leverage their software budgets, achieve the most 
efficient use of their people and of their software assets 
throughout the software lifecycle. It includes three components: 
Software Acquisition Programs, Asset Management Offerings and
Support Services. All Software Utility solutions are customizable to 
meet the individual needs of a customer's unique goals, business 
requirements, platforms and budgets. 

Software Acquisition

     Software Acquisition Programs look to help customers evaluate, 
purchase and install software affordably and with minimum disruption 
to their environments. 

Specific programs include:

     1.	Product Acquisition/Upgrade offerings that enable Digital to 
        provide large corporate users with an easy, cost-effective 
        and flexible ways to make volume purchases of popular 
        business software as well as subscription upgrades. Digital 
        is able to do this through, for example, its participation 
        in Microsoft's Select and Lotus's Passport programs. 
        Together, these programs cover 80 percent of the most 
        popular business applications. 

     2.	Optional Acquisition Service offerings that include 
        electronic software acquisition and delivery. Customers who 
        take advantage of these services can eliminate costs related 
        to processing purchase orders. In addition, they now have 
        access to just-in-time delivery of software. 

Cradle-to-Grave Software Asset Management Services 

     These services help customers gain better control over their 
software assets, thereby enabling a company to make better use of 
its software purchases. Software Asset Management offerings include 
electronic software distribution capabilities as well as integrated 
tools for automating configuration and asset management tasks for a 
broad range of platforms across the enterprise network.

Specific elements include: 

     1.	POLYCENTER AssetWORKS, an integrated Windows NT management 
        tool that extends the capability of Microsoft's System's 
        Management Server by adding support for multivendor UNIX and 
        OpenVMS platforms as well as providing a robust reporting 
        capability.

     2.	The POLYCENTER portfolio of tools that provide distribution 
        and inventory management functions across OpenVMS and OSF/1 
        client/server environments. The newest offering is 
        POLYCENTER Manager on NetView for Windows NT, an 
        industrial-strength system and network management platform 
        for the Windows NT environment.  POLYCENTER Manager on 
        NetView and POLYCENTER AssetWORKS are an integrated solution 
        that provides automated managing solutions that can reduce 
        costs, reduce manual labor and help customers controls and 
        manage thousands of systems -- local or remote -- from a 
        single system. 

Support Services

     In addition, Software Utility includes a number of support 
services that are based on tightly coupling a variety of Digital's 
capabilities into a customized solution. 

These include: 

     1. HelpDesk services
     2. User Application training and support 
     3. Software publishing

     Any and all of the above can be outsourced, freeing up a 
company's IT staff to focus its efforts on more strategic areas. 

     All Software Utility products and services are sold directly 
through Digital's Multivendor Customer Services organization. In 
addition, a number are available through indirect channels as well. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in managed 
open client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
