            DIGITAL ANNOUNCES INDUSTRY'S FIRST INTEGRATED
        SYSTEM AND NETWORK MANAGEMENT PLATFORMS ON WINDOWS NT


LAS VEGAS, Nevada -- November 15, 1994 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation today announced the industry's first integrated 
multivendor system and network management platforms on Windows NT.  
These platforms provide a robust PC-based environment for the 
delivery of enterprise management solutions. 

     For hardware and software system management, Digital announced  
the availability of POLYCENTER AssetWORKS -- an extension of the 
management scope of Microsoft's Systems Management Server (SMS) to 
multivendor UNIX and OpenVMS systems.  For open network management, 
Digital announced the availability of a software developers' kit for 
POLYCENTER Manager on NetView for Windows NT Workstation -- a port 
of the industry-leading NetView network management platform, jointly 
developed by Digital and IBM.  

     AssetWORKS and NetView have also been designed to interoperate 
as peers, sharing information and moving easily between 
applications.  This combined platform is an industry first, 
establishing Digital as the leader in providing enterprise 
management solutions on Windows NT.

     "Our major customers are embracing Windows NT and need 
industrial strength management applications.  This announcement is 
our first step in delivering comprehensive management solutions for 
Windows NT," said Nancy Strecker, vice president, Digital Software 
Products.  "These exciting new POLYCENTER products demonstrate 
Digital's continued leadership in managing open client/server 
environments."

     "Our customers are looking for integrated management tools for 
their enterprise.  Combining System Management Server, a 
comprehensive solution for managing distributed PCs, with other 
world-class tools, such as POLYCENTER AssetWORKS and POLYCENTER 
Manager on NetView for Windows NT Workstation, results in a 
powerful, integrated, enterprise management solution," said Jim 
Allchin, senior vice president of Microsoft's Business Systems 
Division.

Managing enterprise system and software assets 

     POLYCENTER AssetWORKS makes it easy for customers to gain 
control of their hardware and software investments, and reduce 
operating costs.  AssetWORKS is a Windows NT Workstation application 
based on Microsoft's Systems Management Server which extends the 
inventory and software distribution and installation capabilities to 
multivendor UNIX systems -- SunOS, Solaris, AIX, HP-UX, DEC OSF/1, 
and ULTRIX -- and OpenVMS. 

     AssetWORKS also enhances SMS by providing easy-to-use 
pre-defined and customizable reports.  These reports include system 
inventory, software by system, system by software, job status and 
many others.  All data is consolidated in an SQL database to all for 
easy customization.

     POLYCENTER AssetWORKS utilizes the same easy-to-use graphical 
user interface as SMS, and adds the new UNIX and OpenVMS clients and 
reporting capabilities.  The other SMS clients include a wide range 
of PCs -- MS-DOS, Windows, Windows NT Workstation, OS/2, and 
Macintosh -- and networked server environments -- NetWare, LAN 
Manager, PATHWORKS, Windows for Workgroups, and Windows NT Server.  
It also supports wide area networking protocols such as TCP/IP, 
DECnet, IPX/SPX, ISDN, SNA, and X.25.  In combination, AssetWORKS 
and SMS provide configuration management for all desktops and 
servers. 

     AssetWORKS is part of the Software Utility, a partnership with 
customers to bring flexible solutions to the challenges of managing 
software and hardware assets.  The Software Utility provides 
leading-edge tools and services to help customers leverage their 
software budgets, achieve the most efficient utilization of their 
people and software assets from acquisition to retirement.

     POLYCENTER AssetWORKS will be available in December, 1994 on 
both Intel and Alpha processors.  An AssetWORKS and SMS server 
packaged together is priced at $1500.  Agent prices vary from $25 to 
$250 depending on the number of agents purchased and the operating 
systems supported.  

Industrial strength network management from a PC

     POLYCENTER Manager on NetView for Windows NT Workstation is 
based on the NetView product jointly developed by Digital and IBM 
which currently runs on OSF/1, AIX, and Solaris.  POLYCENTER Manager 
on NetView for Windows NT Workstation combines the ease-of-use of 
Windows 95 style with NetView's award-winning MOTIF graphical user 
interface (GUI) to enhance its usability. 

     The software developer's kit for POLYCENTER Manager on NetView 
for Windows NT Workstation will be available in December at no cost 
through the NetView Association, which recently expanded its support 
to include Windows NT.

     This announcement meets the needs of UNIX and Windows 
management application developers who want to make the move to 
support Windows NT.  UNIX vendors are attracted to the large market 
opportunity which the Windows NT platform provides.  Windows vendors 
are looking for the horsepower to scale their applications to do 
management of fast-growing campus, wide area, and enterprise 
environments.  The Windows NT software developers kit will give 
applications vendors the tools to integrate their applications with 
an industrial strength network management platform.

Integrated Windows NT management platform

     Together, POLYCENTER AssetWORKS and POLYCENTER Manager on 
NetView provide powerful functionality for both system and network 
management.  The interoperability between these products is on a 
peer-to-peer level, with each application sharing information with 
the other, and utilizes the open APIs which provide the critical 
ability to create a very tightly integrated management solution.  
Developers can choose to use these same mechanisms for a tight level 
of integration or may choose to use simpler approaches such as 
launching their applications.

New NetView Association members for Windows NT

     In response to the recent expansion of the NetView Association 
to Windows NT, Digital announced that over 15 vendors have signed 
contracts to port their applications to Windows NT.  

     The NetView Association is jointly sponsored by Digital and IBM 
and is a full-service direct support program for independent network 
and systems management application, SNMP MIB, and service vendors 
who support the NetView products.  Services include loaner software, 
technical support, training, product qualification testing, 
distribution of vendor-specific SNMP MIBs, plus marketing and trade 
show support.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in managed 
open client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
