               ANNOUNCE LICENSING OF HIGH PERFORMANCE
                     FORTRAN COMPILER TECHNOLOGY


      ...SofTech, Licensing its Compiler Technology to Digital
          in 1991, Will Develop Compilers Based on Digital
                   Fortran 90 Enhanced Technology


WASHINGTON, DC -- November 15, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and SofTech, Inc. (OTC: SOFT) today that SofTech, Inc. will license 
Fortran 90 and High Performance Fortran compiler language technology 
from Digital in order to develop enhance its own product line 
currently under development. 

     Digital originally licensed the technology from COMPASS, Inc., 
a subsidiary of SofTech, in 1991. Digital extended and productized 
the technology in its High Performance Fortran 90 compiler, for 
use with Alpha systems, scalable parallel SMP servers and 
AdvantageCluster distributed memory systems. Digital is demonstrat-
ing these products at the IEEE/ACM Supercomputing '94 conference in 
Washington, DC, November 14-18, 1994.     

     "This agreement indicates that the market for high performance 
compilers has reached a level where technology cross-licensing to 
create widespread application compatibility is viewed as a business 
opportunity, rather than as a liability," said SofTech president and 
CEO Norman Rasmussen. "The SofTech/Compass legacy of providing leading 
customer tools and technologies for developers will now be brought to 
the open market. It is SofTech's intention to market high performance 
development tools and environments aggressively in order to encourage 
cross-platform, vendor-independent solution in both technical and 
commercial markets." 

     "Digital has taken SofTech's COMPASS'S technology, proven in 
compiler from Alliant, MasPar, Thinking Machines, and others, and 
developed the first full High Performance Fortran 90 compiler." said 
John O'Keefe, vice president of UNIX Systems Marketing for Digital. 
"We are committed to open systems and language standards, and under 
this agreement SofTech will develop compilers for customers that are 
language compatible with such an excellent product."

     SofTech is licensing Digital's improvements to the COMPASS 
technology to provide its customers language compatibility with 
Digital's implementation of Hi Performance Fortran 90. This 
implementation provides the full Fortran 90 standard as well as 
statement, library, and directive extensions from High Performance 
Fortran (HPF) and a number of extensions defined by Digital Fortran 
implementation of Fortran 77.

     Compared with the old Fortran 77 standard, the Fortran 90 
standard defines a larger, more feature-rich language including 
array syntax, modules, dynamic storage allocation, derived data 
types, and a large set of intrinsic functions that provides 
productivity improvements for the scientific community.

     The HPF extensions support portable and scalable data parallel 
programming on a wide variety of hardware architectures and include 
data placement directives, the FORALL construct, a collection of 
standard library procedures, and a procedure call mechanism 
supporting an interface between High Performance Fortran's data 
parallel computing model and other models, such as message passing.
It is these extensions which allow Fortran 90 programs to be 
decomposed during compilation so that they can be executed in 
parallel on multiple processors.

     SofTech, Inc. has been solving complex business problems for 
its clients since its inception in 1969, through the application of 
sophisticated software technology and state-of-the-art project 
management techniques.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
