        DIGITAL AND XEROX ANNOUNCE $4.3 MILLION CONTRACT WITH
                     ANCHORAGE TELEPHONE UTILITY


            Strategic Alliance Offers "One-Stop Shopping"
 

PHOENIX, Arizona -- November 6, 1994 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation and Xerox Corporation today announced a $4.3 million 
joint contract to provide Anchorage Telephone Utility (ATU) with 
Digital's VAX 4600 systems and a Xerox 4890 color printer.  The 
contract was established under the Enterprise Production Printing 
(EPP) Strategic Alliance, formed last November, to enable Digital 
and Xerox to optimize service to large vertical industries with 
specialized needs.  The announcement was made at the XPLOR '94 
Conference, which opened here today at the Phoenix Convention 
Center.

     ATU, the largest telephone company in the United States in 
terms of geographic area, will be able to increase productivity and 
streamline business operations because of the new computer systems.  
ATU will be able to provide better service to customers by quickly 
printing customer billings and two-sided reports and more 
efficiently handling support functions such as service order, 
billing, trouble shooting, plant records, directory assistance 
calls, and accounting tasks.

     "The EPP Strategic Alliance enables our customers to achieve 
seamless interoperability within their computing environments 
through 'one-stop shopping,'" said Larry Cabrinety, Vice 
President of Digital's Components and Peripherals Business Unit.  
"The fully integrated solutions that result from the Alliance 
support both information processing and document production needs in 
enterprise-wide, networked computing environments."

     "We needed a solution that was flexible enough to develop our 
own billing format and that didn't require a great deal of 
reprogramming of the City's approval process," explained Gary 
Carpenter, network project administrator, at Anchorage Telephone 
Utility.  "The Digital/Xerox system streamlines our billing system 
and provides our customers with comprehensive, easy-to-
understand invoices."

     The Alliance provides joint sales, marketing, customer support 
and cooperative engineering development to achieve interoperability 
and connectivity between computer systems.  Specifically, these 
systems include Digital's VAX and Alpha systems using the OpenVMS 
operating system and printing to Xerox 4850, 4890 and 4135 
production laser printers.  

     "EPP Strategic Alliance enables Xerox to obtain new business in 
previously  'non-Xerox markets'," said Richard Hamje, Xerox printing 
systems marketing executive.  "The Alliance enables us to initiate 
prospective sales because of the Digital representatives' 
recommendations.  That kind of endorsement is critical to our 
business success."

