and merchants to do business on the Internet, once again reaffirming 
that the Internet is open for business.  Digital sees the Internet 
as a cost-effective way to work closely with customers and partners. 
This includes making Digital's systems available for remote access 
over the Internet." 

     "Digital's worldwide reach will bring our open and secure 
products to customers around the globe who want to create and manage 
commercial sites on the Internet," said James H. Clark, chairman and 
CEO of Netscape Communications.  "The availability of full, 
integrated and secure hardware and software solutions makes it easy 
for businesses of all kinds to take advantage of the Internet as the 
new global channel for communications and commerce."

     The Netscape Navigator and Netsite server line bring secure 
communications, performance and support to companies and individuals 
who want to create or access information services on global 
networks.  The products offer easy-to-use interfaces for serving and 
accessing multimedia information on the net, including formatted 
text, graphics, audio, and video.  They employ a hypertext linking 
system that lets users simply click on a word or image to retrieve 
information wherever it is located on the network.  The products are 
fully compatible with other HTTP-based clients and servers. 

     Digital will be the first company offering traditional services
 on the Netscape products worldwide.  This includes 7x24 phone 
support, startup and consulting, media, documentation and rights to 
new versions.  Digital and Netscape will work together on defining 
future product requirements and are collaborating on work going on 
within Digital today to maximize product strengths for both 
companies.

     "Digital is forming partnerships with such companies as 
Netscape Communications to provide the best possible solutions for 
customers," said Giordano.  "We are building a broad set of 
Internet-related products and services, making all of our platforms 
'Internet-ready', and sharing what we have learned from our own 
creative use of the Internet."  The OSF Netsite and Netscape 
products will be available Dec.'94.                                      

     Netscape Communications Corporation is a premier provider of 
open software to enable people and companies to exchange information 
and conduct commerce over the Internet and other global networks.  
The company was founded in April 1994 by Dr. James H. Clark, founder 
of Silicon Graphics, Inc., a Fortune 500 computer systems company; 
and Marc Andreessen, creator of the NCSA Mosaic research prototype 
for the Internet.  Privately held, Netscape Communications 
Corporation is based in Mountain View, California.

