               DIGITAL NAMES FORTUNATO VICE PRESIDENT
                AND GENERAL MANAGER FOR ASIA PACIFIC
                   PERSONAL COMPUTER BUSINESS UNIT


MAYNARD, Mass. -- November 1, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that Frank S. Fortunato has been named vice 
president and general manager, Asia Pacific, for the Personal 
Computer Business Unit, based in Hong Kong.

     Fortunato is responsible for all sales and marketing aspects of 
the Personal Computer Business Unit in the Asia Pacific area and 
reports directly to Bernhard Auer, vice president and general 
manager of Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit.

     "As the Asia Pacific grows in sales and importance to Digital's 
personal computer business we wanted to put a leader in the region 
to guide that growth," commented Bernhard Auer, vice president and 
general manager of Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit.  
"Frank's experience and management skills will help ensure that 
Digital's tremendous growth continues."

     Fortunato has more than 25 years of international experience in 
the information technology industry and has held positions in 
general management, sales, marketing, and service management.  Most 
recently, he was director, Desktop Systems, for the PC Business 
Unit's Asia Pacific area, responsible for the company's line of 
desktop products.

     He joined Digital in 1985 as service operations manager for the 
U.S. Customer Services organization, where he was responsible for 
strategic planning and productivity programs.  In 1989 he moved to 
the Asia Pacific organization as manager, Customer Services for 
desktop services and in 1991 was promoted to director, Desktop 
Systems, where he played a leading role in introducing Digital's 
first personal computers in the Asia Pacific area.

     Prior to joining Digital, Fortunato held several senior 
management positions, including general manager of ITT Data 
Equipment & Systems Division; general manager, Service Division, at 
Elscint, Inc.; and director of operations at Simplex Corporation.

     Fortunato has a master's degree in Electrical Engineering from 
Brooklyn Polytechnical Institute and a bachelor of science degree in 
Physics from Adelphi University.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
