                DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION EXPANDS
              STORAGE PLATFORM AND ENVIRONMENT SUPPORT


      StorageWorks Solutions Now Available For Hewlett-Packard,
                         IBM, and Windows NT


MAYNARD, Mass. -- November 1, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced expanded storage support for multivendor UNIX and PC 
Network environments.  Digital's StorageWorks line of disk, tape and 
optical storage products is now available for Hewlett-Packard and 
IBM UNIX-based systems, and for Intel based PCs and servers running 
the Microsoft Windows NT 32-bit operating system.  The expansion 
demonstrates a long-term commitment to provide a complete line of 
StorageWorks products for heterogeneous computing environments.

     According to Paul Feresten, vice president of sales and 
marketing for Digital's Storage Business Unit, "New StorageWorks 
support for HP, IBM and Windows NT is the latest indication of our 
intent to deliver on the StorageWorks vision: to provide enterprise-
wide storage solutions in multivendor environments with a line of 
high-performance, flexible, scalable, modular products.  No other
company supports more open platforms, with a line of desktop to 
datacenter storage products, than Digital.  With today's 
increasingly complex, multiple vendor information systems 
installations, this cross-platform capability is mandatory."

     Paul Goldman, president of ARQANA Technologies, Inc., a 
StorageWorks reseller, stated, "StorageWorks products are already 
unique in providing a true multiplatform storage architecture.  Our 
customers realize the importance of this standard backbone as they 
move storage to increasingly complex computer systems.  For users 
seeking to maximize their investment protection, new StorageWorks 
support for HP, IBM, and Windows NT is wonderful news."

     Kirby Wadsworth, manager of StorageWorks product marketing, 
added, "It is a testament to the inherent StorageWorks compatibility 
with open systems that many customers already use our products in 
HP, IBM, and NT environments.  We now offer fully qualified 
solutions backed by the superior service, support, and warranty 
the industry has come to expect from StorageWorks products."

StorageWorks Solutions for Hewlett-Packard, IBM, and Windows NT

     StorageWorks offers a full line of disk, tape and optical 
storage products for HP, IBM and Windows NT environments.  These 
products are compatible with HP 9000/700 and HP 9000/800 systems 
running HP-UX, IBM RS/6000 systems running AIX, and Intel based 
systems running Windows NT Versions 3.1 or 3.5.

     In addition, Windows NT users now can benefit from the 
fault-tolerant data protection of the StorageWorks RAID Array 210.  
Introduced last summer for Novell NetWare users, the RAID Array 210 
controller-based disk array ensures continuous access to critical 
applications.

Pricing and Availability

     StorageWorks prices for Hewlett-Packard, IBM and Windows NT 
environments begin at $1,500.  These products are now available 
exclusively from select value-added resellers (VARs) and 
distributors.  Call 1-800-STORWORKS for more information.

     StorageWorks is a comprehensive family of disk, tape and 
optical storage subsystems, offering modular, competitively-priced, 
industry-standard solutions in customizable desktop, deskside, and 
datacenter enclosures.  StorageWorks products are available on a 
wide range of multivendor environments, including Novell, Sun 
Microsystems, Digital, and now Hewlett-Packard, IBM and Windows NT.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
