          TELKOM SOUTH AFRICA SELECTS NEW ALPHA SYSTEMS AND
      DIGITAL PARTNER SOLUTIONS FOR STRATEGIC SYSTEMS OVERHAUL


    ... Major telecommunications provider stresses powerful Alpha
  technology, future-safe architecture for next 10 to 20 years ...


JOHANNESBURG, SOUTH AFRICA -- November 2, 1994 -- Telkom South 
Africa has selected Digital and its business partners to provide the 
heart of the telecommunications provider's Client Business System 
(CBS). CBS -- Telkom's nationwide, computerized customer support and 
billing system -- is central to Telkom South Africa's strategic, 
three-year business reengineering effort. Through the project, 
Telkom South Africa will substantially improve service to both 
private and corporate clients, and become better equipped to 
successfully compete with leading international telecommunications 
companies. 

     The contract, valued between $15 and $18 million over the next 
three years, calls for Digital and its business partners to build an 
information infrastructure based on Digital's 64-bit Alpha 
workstations and servers, and DEC OSF/1 operating system (Digital's 
UNIX). 

     "CBS represents one of the most significant IT systems ever 
developed for Telkom and will be one of the largest UNIX based 
client/server implementations in South Africa," said Nic van Rooyen, 
Telkom's general manager, Support Division. "Digital's Alpha 
architecture provides the performance and growth capabilities 
central to the project's success, given its critical nature and 
planned evolution over the next 10 to 20 years."

Strategic Partnerships Deliver More Than Sum of Parts

     "This project highlights the value of close working 
relationships between Digital, its strategic business partners and 
leading companies such as and Oracle at the engineering level," said 
Al Peters, general manager, Digital South Africa.  The information 
technology portion of CBS will be delivered via a partnership 
between three companies in South Africa. The prime contractor, 
BSW-Data, is a South Africa systems integrator and solutions 
provider to the telecommunications industry. Digital South Africa is 
the local subsidiary of Digital Equipment Corporation and provider 
of the Alpha computer systems, DEC OSF/1 operating system and 
various support services. Sofrecom/France Telecom, a Paris-based 
telecommunications software provider and part of France Telecom, 
is the French telephone operating company. Sofrecom will implement 
its Giraffe 2G software.

     The Giraffe 2G application will use the Oracle 7.1 database 
optimized for Digital's 64-bit Alpha technology. "The combination 
has demonstrated distinct performance advantages in independent 
benchmark and other performance tests," added Peters.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
                                ####

