  ...Tailored for Volume Selling by Partners...


              DIGITAL'S ALPHA SALVO SCORES DIRECT HIT;
              EIGHT-SYSTEM LINEUP BLANKETS COMPETITION


  ...AlphaGeneration Systems Deliver Industry-Leading Performance...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- November 3, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation
today introduced new lines of Alpha workstations and server systems
for open client/server computing that boast the industry's best
performance and price/performance. 

     The AlphaStation and AlphaServer lines are the industry's first 
to incorporate advanced 64-bit microprocessor technology with 
PC-style advantages such as the industry-standard PCI bus.  More 
than 6,400 applications are available, with a choice of  operating 
systems including DEC OSF/1 (UNIX), OpenVMS, and for the first time,
Microsoft's Windows NT across both lines. 

     Sales of the new systems will be enhanced by Digital's new 
channels focus. Starting today, Digital's partners will begin 
showcasing the new systems to thousands of customers at events in 
175 locations worldwide. 
Added Value, More Choice 

     "Digital's AlphaStation and AlphaServer systems deliver 
leadership price/performance for customers and  partners," said 
Enrico Pesatori, vice president and general manager, Computer 
Systems Division. "They offer more value by combining high-end 
performance and reliability with the low-cost design of PCs.  
Not only do these systems cost less to buy, they cost less to own.  
Customers can choose from a range of servers and workstations that 
are scalable to their needs, and can buy from sales channels that 
suit their business and service requirements.

     "For our growing network of channels partners, we are 
introducing simplified business practices, aggressive joint 
advertising campaigns, and comprehensive support programs," 
Pesatori added. 

Alpha System Lineup 

     Ranging from low-end clients to high-capacity enterprise 
servers, the new Alpha offerings extend Digital's price/performance 
leadership in the most rapidly growing market segments:  the $10,000 
to $15,000 workstation range, low and mid-range servers, and 
mainframe-alternative systems.  High-end models are based on the 
Alpha 21064A microprocessor, the world's fastest in volume 
production. 

The new Alpha systems begin shipping this month.  Three Alpha
workstations and five Alpha servers are offered: 

     *  AlphaStation 200 4/166 and AlphaStation 200 4/233 mid-range 
     	desktop workstations

     *  AlphaStation 400 4/233 mini-tower workstation

     *  AlphaServer 1000 4/200 entry-level server

     *  AlphaServer 2000 4/200 entry-level multiprocessing server

     *  AlphaServer 2100 4/275 high-end SMP departmental server

     *  AlphaServer 2100 4/275 high-end SMP departmental server 
        (cabinet version) 

     *  DEC 7000 Model 700 multiprocessor enterprise server

     As part of today's announcement, Digital introduced new 
AlphaServer and AlphaStation trademarks, and renamed its highly 
successful Digital 2100 A500MP server as the AlphaServer 2100 4/200 
system. 

Builds on Performance Lead 

     Philippe Ribeyre, vice president, Workstation Business Segment, 
Alpha Systems Business Group, commenting on the new workstations'
performance said, "The  AlphaStation 200 4/166 is 70 percent faster
than the IBM 25T, offering the highest UNIX  performance customers 
can buy in the $10,000 range.  It also provides a high-performance
alternative to Intel platforms.  Running Windows NT Workstation, it
delivers 79 percent more floating-point performance than 90MHz 
Pentium systems.  The AlphaStation 200 4/233 desktop and 
AlphaStation 400 4/233 mini-tower set a new performance standard in 
the $15,000 range.  They surpass HP's 715/80 and IBM's 41T system 
speeds by 50-80 percent and up to 75 percent, respectively," Ribeyre 
added. 

     "AlphaServer performance also beats comparable IBM, HP, and Sun
offerings," according to Pauline Nist, vice president, Server 
Business Segment, Alpha Systems  Business Group.  "The entry-level 
AlphaServer 1000 4/200 outperforms the HP 9000-800 E55, the IBM 
PowerServer 390, the Sun SPARCserver 20, and the Compaq Proliant 
1000 by 20-60 percent.  The AlphaServer 2000 4/200 is twice as fast 
as the HP G50 at a lower price, and 75 percent faster than the IBM 
RS/6000-G30 dual CPU for 60 percent of the price.  

Similarly, the AlphaServer 2100 4/275 delivers up to twice the speed 
of the HP I70 for the same price, and up to 50 percent more 
performance than the Sun SPARCserver 1000E and IBM 59H at two-thirds 
the price or less. 

     "Our mainframe alternative, the DEC 7000 Model 700 system with 
six processors, outperforms the HP 9000 Model T500 with 12 
processors," Nist added. 

Modeled on AlphaServer 2100 Success 

     New AlphaGeneration systems exploit the design concepts of the 
highly successful  Digital AlphaServer 2100 system introduced in 
April.  This 'breakthrough' server set a  new level in price/
performance by combining Alpha power, symmetric multiprocessing, and 
PC bus technology. 

     Today's new systems incorporate industry-standard Peripheral 
Component Interconnect (PCI), ISA, and EISA bus technologies, 
enabling customers to use many  widely available, off-the-shelf 
peripheral devices.  Further, they incorporate large-system features 
-- high availability, scalability, and reliability -- with small-
system advantages including high-performance graphics, multimedia, 
and PC-style packaging. 

AlphaStation Markets 

     Digital's new AlphaStation systems offer the high-performance 
graphics and network support needed for demanding technical and 
commercial applications including  mechanical CAD, EDA (Electronic 
Design Automation), software engineering, mapping, technical 
publishing, and visualization. AlphaStation systems feature the best 
RISC-based desktop workstation warranty in the industry. 

AlphaStation Pricing 

     Prices (excluding monitor) begin at $6,995 for the AlphaStation 
200 4/166, at $11,750 for the AlphaStation 200 4/233, and at $12,595 
for the AlphaStation 400 4/233 system.  The workstations are 
currently available through an extensive network of Value-Added 
Resellers, OEMs, and distributors, or directly from Digital. 

Best Servers for Critical Tasks 

     "In the current competitive and rapidly changing business 
climate where users are  asked to do more, faster, at less cost, 
they demand systems with quick response times, fast  application 
processing and uninterrupted service.  Digital's new AlphaServer 
systems  emphasize high performance, high availability, and security 
for business-critical commercial and technical applications," said 
Nist. 

     AlphaServer systems are ideal for use as application and 
database servers, especially for finance and accounting, PC LAN 
servers, installed-base cluster  consolidation, and high-performance 
computing.  "The new AlphaServer line offers the industry's best 
RISC-based warranty -- three-year, next-day response.  Their design 
and warranties keep support costs low.  AlphaServer systems are the 
best machines on the market from a cost-of-ownership perspective," 
Nist added. 

     AlphaServer storage subsystems combine reliability and high-
availability features such as controller-based RAID (Redundant
Arrays of Inexpensive Disks), hot-standby and  hot-swap disks, and 
ECC (error-correcting code) main and cache memory -- all within the 
system pedestal.  All AlphaServer systems also feature thermal 
management, automatic restart, and an optional redundant power 
system. 

DEC 7000 Model 700 AXP Server 

     The DEC 7000 Model 700 AXP Server is the industry's most 
powerful enterprise  server and winner for overall performance in 
AIM Technology's 1994 Hot Iron Awards for UNIX Computer Systems.  
Like the AlphaServer 2100 4/275, it incorporates Digital's 275 MHz 
Alpha AXP 21064A chip.  With its six symmetric multiprocessors, the 
DEC 7000 Model 700 boasts performance of an estimated 1,350 
transactions per second and an AIM rating of 643.5 with five CPUs -- 
the highest in the industry.  The new server exceeds SPECint92 and 
SPECfp92 performance of the DEC 7000 Model 600 AXP Server by 40 
percent. 

AlphaServer Pricing 

     Entry-level pricing for AlphaServer systems starts at $15,970 
for the AlphaServer 1000 4/200 system; $18,070 for AlphaServer 2000 
4/200; $21,940 for AlphaServer 2100 4/200; $33,390 for AlphaServer 
2100 4/275, and $120,000 for the DEC 7000 Model 700 AXP system. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
client/server solutions  from personal computing to integrated
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms,
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
