           DIGITAL'S ALPHASTATION AND ALPHASERVER SYSTEMS:
                 'PERFECT PRODUCT SET' FOR PARTNERS


MAYNARD, Mass. -- November 3, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today delivered on its partner-focused strategy with the 
announcement of eight new workstations and servers optimized for 
delivery through Digital's volume sales channels. The new lines of 
AlphaStation and AlphaServer systems designed for open client/server 
computing boast the industry's best performance and price/
performance. 

     These systems offer customers more value by combining large-
system performance and reliability features with the low-cost 
innovations of personal computers.  For customers, this translates 
into systems that not only cost less to buy, but cost less to own. 

     "The new Alpha systems are a perfect product set for our
partners," said Harold D. Copperman, vice president worldwide sales 
and marketing, in Digital's new Systems Business Unit. They are 
enthusiastic about the products and are planning to show them off at 
our partners' customer events in 175 locations around the world. 

     "Digital plans to be the 'partner of preference.'  We are
developing leadership programs to demonstrate that commitment," he 
added. "To date, we have established a competitive discount structure, 
streamlined the terms and conditions of our software contracts, and 
conducted pre-announcement product sales and marketing training 
classes. Further, we have introduced new partner-focused on-line 
support tools, and provided comprehensive support materials for our 
partners' product introduction events," he added. 

     Digital will provide partners the marketing support needed to 
increase demand and broaden the marketshare for Alpha products.  It 
has increased advertising spending significantly and put in place 
joint marketing programs to generate new business for its partners.  
Furthermore, Digital's direct sales managers for large accounts will 
work closely with Digital's partners to provide solutions those 
customers require.  Digital expects 50 percent of this business will 
be sold by its partners.

     "We plan to make it easier for our partners to do business with 
us," Copperman said.  "Our partners have done an excellent job 
selling Digital products this past year, and we intend to make next 
year an even better year for them. 

     "Digital has the leadership products, the leadership sales and 
marketing programs and the determination to make it happen.  
Digital's partners are very enthusiastic about our Alpha advanced 
technology products and our focus on selling more products with 
them.  We will work with our partners to respond to the increased 
demand in the marketplace for Alpha products," Copperman added. 

     In the first quarter of fiscal year 1995, the percentage of 
products sold through Digital's channels rose from 45 to 57 percent.  
The company expects that sales through channels will be more than 60 
percent by the end of fiscal year 1995. 

The following are reactions from some Digital partners about the new 
Alpha lines and working with Digital: 

     "We are seeing a 60-70 percent increase in Alpha sales 
     quarter-to-quarter with the flagship AlphaServer 2100 4/200
     driving the increase, said Pat O'Connor, Senior Corporate
     Marketing Manager for North America at Pioneer-Standard
     Electronics, a distributor with sales of $1.06 billion.
     "Digital's partner programs such as 'Alpha2-Step,' 'Triple
     Trade-in' and 'Advantage Upgrade' are generating new Alpha 
     sales in VAX accounts in addition to new Digital accounts.  
     Digital and Pioneer have a synergistic relationship," he 
     continued. "Our goals are aligned, and together we are 
     delivering tailored solutions for our customers with the Alpha 
     family of products." 

     "The new generation of Alpha AXP servers have truly awesome 
     capabilities and are sized for every application that we sell," 
     said Michael B. Andelman, president of LIOCS Corporation, a 
     leading supplier of turnkey financial, distribution,
     manufacturing and warehouse management systems. "The 
     AlphaServer 1000 and 2000 systems offer power and flexibility 
     allowing us to deliver affordable turnkey solutions for 
     departmental applications like our paperless real-time 
     Warehouse Management systems." 

     "Our sales of Digital's products are up over 80 percent from 
     last year.  Clearly the customer base is recognizing the
     price/performance advantages of Alpha systems," said Josh 
     Napua, Executive Vice President, Computer Products at Wyle 
     Laboratories, a $1 billion, nation-wide electronic distributor. 
     "The number of conversions we see from Sun, Data General, and 
     Wang is increasing very nicely.  Half of our customers, many of 
     them new accounts, choose DEC OSF/1, which is being recognized 
     as a very robust UNIX." 

     "With the new Alpha servers, our resellers can proactively 
     pursue both department and enterprise opportunities," said 
     Sean Fanning, Director of Marketing, Hall-Mark Computer
     Products, a division of AVNET, Inc.  He continued, "In terms of
     technology, Digital is far ahead of anyone else.  Digital is 
     the only company with a universal platform that enables people 
     to run Windows NT, UNIX and Open VMS applications on a single 
     platform.  Digital's 64-bit Alpha servers have leapfrogged 
     competitive servers from a price/performance standpoint." 

