                  DIGITAL AND OPEN MARKET, INC. (OMI) PARTNER
               TO MAKE IT EASIER TO DO BUSINESS OVER THE INTERNET
    
    
                    New Merchant Services Over The Internet


BOSTON, MA -- October 24, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation
today announced its intent to partner with Open Market, Inc. (OMI) to
market StoreBuilder and Merchant Server. With these products and
services, banks can cost-effectively help retail companies conduct
on-line business over the Internet. 
    
     "We see the beginnings of a global electronic mall -- a new 
environment for doing business, which requires new ways of creating 
products, attracting customers, accepting payment and providing 
service," said Rose Ann Giordano, Vice President of Digital's new 
Internet Business Group. "OMI offers products and services which 
complement our own and will enable us to help customers to quickly and 
inexpensively take advantage of the enormous opportunities which are now 
opening." 
  
     Banks are looking for ways to use the Internet to provide
additional services to their retail merchants, and thereby gain
competitive advantage for their merchants and themselves. In addition
banks would like to increase transaction volume from credit card
processing while maintaining strict security measures. OMI provides
banks with a cost-effective way to let their retail merchants open
"stores" on the Internet in the multi-media environment of the
World-Wide Web, with its point-and-click ease of use. 
  
     Open Market, Inc.'s Chief Executive Officer Shikhar Ghosh said, 
"Digital's leadership products combined with Open Market's technologies 
and systems add up to the most comprehensive set of solutions available 
today for conducting commerce over the Internet. Digital is the world's 
leading supplier of 64-bit systems, providing a performance that is 
unparalleled for a wide range of banking applications."
   
     OMI's Store Builder family of products enable a merchant with
little or no experience with electronic commerce to create a store on
the Internet. The product creation tools enable a company to redefine
its product line to take advantage of the efficiencies of electronic 
distribution. OMI's Payment, Security and Authentication system enable 
companies to manage the transaction with the customer in a secure and 
efficient manner using traditional payment instruments. Together these 
offerings provide a secure online environment for transactions.
  
     The principle components of the Open Market system,currently being 
demonstrated at the Digital Stand at the SIBOS exhibition and conference 
in Boston, Massachusetts from October 24-28th are:
  
    o The Store Builder - a do-it-yourself kit that will allow companies
      or individuals to set up a storefront, design their own marquees,
      fill in prices and description of items displayed, add scanned   
      images and open for business on the Internet.
    
    o The Payment Server - connects OMI's buyers and merchants to the
      financial networks. It provides a secure environment for
      transaction processing including real-time authentication and
      authorization for credit card transactions, housing of secure
      merchants accounts, and secure on-line communication for dispute
      resolution.
    
    o The Merchant Server - houses merchants from all over the world,
      and serves as the interface between merchants and buyers allowing
      them to communicate in real-time regarding purchases, customer
      service, and other aspects of commerce.
    
     OMI was founded in 1994 and is funded by venture capital investment 
from Greylock Management and private investors. Initial products and 
services focus on the Internet as the medium for conducting business, 
with future products and services to address additional segments of the 
"Information Superhighway" as they become available.
  
     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha AXP platforms, storage, 
networking, software and services, together with industry-focused 
solutions from business partners, help organizations compete and win in 
today's global marketplace.
