          DIGITAL'S GLOBAL CONTRACT MANUFACTURING SERVICES
               INKS AGREEMENTS WITH RADIUS AND TADPOLE


    ...Newest Contracts Illustrate How OEMs Can Take Advantage Of
         Digital's Worldwide Reach, Full-Service Capabilities
                   and Manufacturing Expertise...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- November 8, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that it has signed two new major contract 
manufacturing agreements with San Jose, California-based Radius, 
Inc. and Cambridge, England-based Tadpole Technology.  The 
agreements were made with Digital's Global Contract Manufacturing 
Services organization.

     According to the agreements, Digital will build Radius's
graphics accelerator cards for the PC market, and communications 
cards for Tadpole.  These most recent agreements fortify the 
organization's growing list of OEM customers who have outsourced 
their manufacturing to Digital, benefiting from the company's 
established worldwide presence, state-of-the-art manufacturing 
facilities, economies of scale, procurement power and logistics 
capabilities. 

      Radius, Inc., a leading developer of color publishing, digital 
video and multimedia products, chose Digital to manufacture its 
graphics accelerator cards at Digital's Augusta, Maine facility.  
After a year-long subcontractor review process, Digital's expansive 
service portfolio was key to Radius' decision to form a contract 
manufacturing partnership.  "Radius is taking advantage of the full 
range of Digital's value-added services," said Mary Godwin, Radius' 
Director of Operations.  "Digital has played an integral role in 
virtually every stage of the manufacturing cycle--helping with 
everything from implementing design for manufacturability, to 
providing repair services," added Godwin. 

      For Tadpole Technology, which specializes in RISC-based 
portable notebook systems, Digital is performing high-density 
assembly and test of Tadpole-designed communications printed circuit 
boards, at its Ayr, Scotland plant.  "Perhaps the most important 
factors that went into our decision to outsource to Digital were 
flexibility and worldwide scope," said Gary Howse, Tadpole's 
Director of Manufacturing.  "We wanted to be sure to choose a 
manufacturing partner we wouldn't outgrow, whose technical and 
manufacturing capabilities will expand to accommodate our future 
product lines," Howse added.  "In addition to that, we found that 
Digital is able to handle the global distribution of the products 
they manufacture for us," concluded Howse. 

       "Global Contract Manufacturing Services aims to provide cost-
effective solutions to OEMs' production and logistics challenges," 
said Jim Willis, Digital's Component OEM Vice President within its 
Components and Peripherals Business Unit. "Radius and Tadpole are 
exemplary of OEMs making the most of Digital's end-to-end services 
by letting Global Contract Manufacturing Services guide them through 
the multi-step manufacturing process."  The organization boasts a 
rapidly-expanding base of OEM customers with varying needs, creating 
new relationships with both young, fast-growing companies and with 
established Fortune 500 corporations. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
