                DIGITAL REDEFINES NOTEBOOK COMPUTERS
                        WITH NEW HINOTE LINE


MAYNARD, Mass. -- November 11, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today entered the fast-growing notebook marketplace with two Digital 
HiNote notebook families that redefine style, portability and 
usability for mobile computer users.  The new families of Digital 
designed notebook computers include five HiNote models and five 
HiNote Ultra models, and feature breakthrough design in the 
lightest, slimmest, full-size, full-feature notebooks on the market.

     "Digital is enhancing how people interact with their 
computers," commented Bernhard Auer, vice president and general 
manager of Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit.  "These HiNote 
notebooks redefine that relationship.  The combination of aesthetic 
and ergonomic design, power, ease-of-use and compatibility makes 
them extremely appealing to resellers and users alike.  With the 
HiNote line as our entry into the fast-growing notebook market, we 
continue our drive to become one of the top five PC vendors by the 
end of 1995."

     "We expect Digital's HiNote notebooks to become an instant 
success with our resellers and customers," added Raymond Weadock, 
vice president and general manager, Americas, for the Digital 
Personal Computer Business Unit.  "Our channel partners who have 
reviewed the new systems see both the HiNote and the HiNote Ultra 
notebooks as ideal additions to their product portfolios."

     The Digital HiNote line is designed to provide excellent 
performance, reliability and ease-of use in a lightweight, sleek 
design -- at a competitive price.  The HiNote systems are targeted 
at mobile users such as sales and service personnel and others who 
work out of the office, such as insurance and healthcare 
professionals, journalists and consultants.

     The HiNote Ultra family redefines mobile computing, combining 
the latest technology in the sleekest, most ergonomic and attractive 
form factor on the market.  At under four pounds with a full 9.5 
inch screen, infrared communications, business audio, and the latest 
in notebook technology, the HiNote Ultra is the first "no sacrifice" 
notebook for  the mobile professional who must have a powerful, 
portable, presentable system at all times.

     Both HiNote and HiNote Ultra notebooks feature an innovative, 
centered, built-in trackball with a surround click button for left- 
and right-handed users; a sculpted palm rest for comfort; a 
full-size 82-key keyboard with 19mm key pitch and 3mm key travel for 
the touch and feel of a desktop keyboard; and quick release PCMCIA 
eject buttons that make it easy to hot swap communications, network, 
storage and multimedia options.

     Digital also announced Digital branded PCMCIA HiNote notebook 
system options including FAX/modems; Ethernet and Token Ring network 
connectors; SCSI cards; hard disk storage cards and multimedia cards 
that are fully tested with the HiNote line and warranted to be fully 
compatible.  All Digital branded and third party PCMCIA cards, as 
well as other options, are easy to add and remove since the new 
notebooks feature Plug and Play Flash BIOS and are Microsoft Windows 
95 Ready.  

     In addition, an LCD status panel next to the screen informs 
users of battery life, disk access, communications status and 
several critical functions.  All HiNote and HiNote Ultra options, 
such as AC adapters, carry the same breakthrough design concepts in 
light, attractive packages giving HiNote and HiNote Ultra notebooks 
the lightest travel weight in the industry.

HiNote -- Puts Real Value Back into the "Value" Segment

     The Digital HiNote family sets new standards for what the 
industry has defined as the value segment of the notebook market.  
It combines innovative design in five value models, all featuring 
full-sized, 82 key keyboards and 9.5 inch display screens in an 8.5 
x 11 inch form factor.  The HiNote 433 dual scan STN monochrome 
weighs only 4.9 pounds and measures just 1.5 inches high.  The 
HiNote CS 433 and CS 450 dual scan STN color models weigh only 5.4 
pounds, and the high-end HiNote CT 450 and CT 475 TFT active matrix 
color models weigh just 5.5 pounds; the color models measure only 
1.7 inches high.  U.S. list prices range from $1699 to $4399.

     "We focused on what business professionals want in their 
notebook computers," said Winnie Briney, vice president, mobile 
systems for Digital's PC Business Unit.  "That's why we designed the 
HiNote system to be light and attractive but with full power and 
functionality with pre-loaded software that traveling professionals 
need."

     In addition, HiNote features up to 1MB video memory and 32-bit 
local bus video for outstanding color graphics performance and 
full-motion video; two hot-swappable, PCMCIA slots on the color 
models; Enhanced Parallel Port; user upgradeable 120, 240, 340MB 
hard drives; and advanced power management features that give up to 
six hours of battery life under normal usage.

     HiNote options include a standard Port Replicator and a PCMCIA 
Port Replicator that allows up to a total of four PCMCIA slots, a 
hot-swappable spare battery, car adapter and battery charger.

HiNote Ultra - Redefines Mobile Computing

     The HiNote Ultra notebook is unique from the first look.  Small 
size and light weight, without sacrificing a full size keyboard and 
large 9.5 inch screen, are central design criteria.  The 8.5 x 11 
inch HiNote Ultra 433 dual scan STN monochrome is just 1 inch high, 
and weights only 3.5 pounds.  The color models measure only 1.2 
inches in height. The dual-scan STN color HiNote Ultra CS 433 and 
450 models weigh only 3.9 pounds and the TFT active matrix color 
HiNote Ultra CT 450 and CT 475 come in at 4 pounds. This makes the 
HiNote Ultra family, by far, the lightest, most compact, full-size, 
notebook computer on the market.  The HiNote Ultra family is priced 
between $2099 and $4999 in the U.S.

     "Our team of expert notebook engineers and designers threw out 
conventional thinking when they created the HiNote Ultra," said 
Briney.  "They designed a notebook computer that literally breaks 
the mold on power and size, look and feel, and how they fit into a 
professional's work style.  Customers, resellers and analysts who 
have seen early HiNote Ultra models have been unanimously 
enthusiastic, and immediately wanted one."

     It is the first notebook with an integral Lithium Ion battery 
that flips down to tilt the unit to a comfortable typing angle.  The 
HiNote Ultra also includes an innovative, "zero footprint," 
wedge-shaped, hot-dockable floppy disk drive that clips directly 
onto the system in the open space under the notebook created by the 
flip down battery.  This unique floppy dock requires no cables and 
operates like an integrated floppy drive.  In addition, a full-size 
keyboard, ambidextrous trackball and LCD status panel are standard on 
the HiNote Ultra.

     The notebooks are optimized for demanding mobile users. The 
flip-down, hot-swappable Lithium Ion battery delivers up to six 
hours under normal usage, providing the longest battery life per 
pound in the industry.  A built-in infrared port allows quick and 
easy wireless communications with similarly equipped personal 
computers and printers for the most efficient integration of mobile 
computing with office applications. HiNote Ultra systems with Intel 
DX2/50 and DX4/75 processors include 16-bit business audio for 
multimedia applications and presentations, and 1MB of video memory.  
The HiNote Ultra 433 and 450 models are user upgradeable to the 
DX4/75 processor.

     In addition, HiNote Ultra includes 170, 240 or 340MB factory 
upgradeable hard drives, quick-release PCMCIA slots with convenient 
release buttons for fast, hot swaps of option cards; a serial port 
and an ECP/EPP parallel port, Plug and Play Flash BIOS; a small, 1 
inch high AC adapter; and the removable floppy dock.  Options 
include a snap-on PCMCIA "zero footprint" wedge-shaped expansion 
dock to support up to a total of four PCMCIA cards -- the most in 
the industry.
HiNote and HiNote Ultra - Optimized for the Business User

     The HiNote line includes MS-DOS 6.22, Windows for Workgroups 
3.11 and Digital's "Getting Started" user interface to help users 
become productive quickly with their new systems.  In the U.S. the 
full HiNote line is Internet ready using Delphi"s InterNav Internet 
navigation software.  The HiNote line also includes several other 
application packages for mobile professionals, including Lotus 
Organizer, CompuServe, OAG FlightDisk and Second Nature Screen 
Saver.

     HiNote and HiNote Ultra are covered by Digital's worldwide 
three-year limited warranty.  Digital's Passport service, offering 
seven day - 24 hour, toll free phone support with 48-hour repair and 
free courier pick up and delivery service, is offered free-of-charge 
for the first year in the U.S., and is optional in other countries.

     HiNote and HiNote Ultra notebooks use Intel's 3.3 volt SL 
enhanced Intel SX33, DX2/50 and DX4/75 processors and include 4MB 
RAM, expandable to 20MB (8MB expandable to 24MB in the HiNote Ultra 
CT 450 and CT 475).  The company also stated that 520MB hard drive 
HiNote and HiNote Ultra models and upgrades, as well as 
CD-ROM/Multimedia expansion docks for the HiNote Ultra, will be 
available in the Spring of 1995.

     HiNote notebooks are available in November and HiNote Ultra 
systems will be available in December from Digital and authorized 
resellers.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
