           DIGITAL ANNOUNCES REIMBURSABLE WARRANTY PROGRAM
                   FOR HARDCOPY AND VIDEO PRODUCTS


LAS VEGAS, Nevada -- November 14, 1994 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation today announced its Authorized Warranty Service Provider 
Program (AWSP), a reimbursable warranty program for its full line of 
printer and video products.  The program enables Digital's retail 
and VAR resellers of these products to provide warranty service to 
their customers, and be reimbursed directly from Digital.  The 
announcement was made at the COMDEX show, which opened here today at 
the Las Vegas Convention Center.

     "Digital has a strong reputation as a service provider for its 
hardcopy and video products, and offers two- and three-year 
warranties on many of them," said Patrick Sullivan, Merchandising 
Business Vice President in Digital's Components and Peripherals 
Business Unit.  "This new AWSP program enables customers to obtain 
warranty service from the retailer or VAR from whom they purchased 
the product, in their local area.  This program will expand 
Digital's service capabilities by expanding the locations providing 
warranty service and is another step in continuing to meet customer 
needs with our partners."

     The launch of AWSP will result in a number of resellers 
qualifying to provide warranty service.  The names of these service 
providers will be announced at a later date.

     The program includes all of Digital's hardcopy products, text 
and X Window terminals, and Multia desktop. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation, is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
